cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Temari: relativistic off-diagonal inner-shell ionization form factors for STEM-EDX and ALCHEMI"
message: "If you use this software or the tables it generates, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Seto
    given-names: Yusuke
    email: seto77@gmail.com
    # 260811Cl: 統合前の .github/CITATION.cff にだけ入っていた所属を引き継いだ
    affiliation: "Osaka Metropolitan University, Japan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/seto77/Temari"
url: "https://seto77.github.io/Temari/"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/seto77/Temari/blob/main/licenses/README.md"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
keywords:
  - electron microscopy
  - EELS
  - STEM-EDX
  - ALCHEMI
  - inner-shell ionization
  - ionization form factor
  - mixed dynamic form factor
  - generalized oscillator strength
  - atomic form factor
  - electron scattering
  - Dirac-Hartree-Fock-Slater
  - Julia
abstract: >-
  Temari computes and publishes the off-diagonal inner-shell ionization form
  factor F(s, E0) that quantitative STEM-EDX and ALCHEMI need: the mixed
  dynamic form factor contracted over the ejected electron's energy and
  direction, for two Bloch waves separated by K = 4*pi*s*a0, then normalized at
  K = 0. It solves an isolated atom from scratch — self-consistent field, bound
  orbitals and distorted continuum waves — and derives from that one atom the
  scattering and excitation factors used by electron microscopy, spectroscopy
  and transport simulation: besides F(s, E0), the EELS differential cross
  section, the generalized oscillator strength, X-ray
  and electron atomic scattering factors, and Mott elastic cross sections. It
  depends on the Julia standard library only and contains no fitted parameter
  tables, with one declared exception (the public-domain Bote–Salvat ionization
  cross-section coefficients; see CONTRIBUTING.md). Generated datasets carry
  their own version, independent of this software version, are distributed
  separately under CC-BY-4.0 while the software itself is MIT, and each is
  pinned to a specific Julia release in its manifest. The prescription was chosen and
  verified by the author; the bulk of the implementation was written by an AI
  assistant (Anthropic Claude) under that direction.
references:
  # 260811Cl: CFF 1.2.0 の reference type に "dataset" は無い (正しくは "data")。
  # 誤った型名だとファイル全体が schema 検証に落ち、GitHub の "Cite this repository" が出ない。
  # ⚠ Zenodo 側の resource type は "Dataset" が正しい — 語彙が別なので合わせないこと。
  - type: data
    title: >-
      Inner-shell ionization form factors F(s, E0) for STEM-EDX: 525 channels
      (K, L1-L3, M1-M5) computed with Temari
    authors:
      - family-names: Seto
        given-names: Yusuke
    version: "5.0.0"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21872050"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: >-
      Dataset v5.0.0, released separately from this software and under different
      terms (CC-BY-4.0; the software is MIT). Cite this version DOI for
      reproducibility -- it guarantees the files have not changed. The
      version-independent DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21872049 resolves to the latest
      version instead. A byte-identical mirror is attached to the GitHub release
      dataset-v5.0.0; the archive is built deterministically so the two copies
      can be compared rather than merely trusted.
  # 260817Cl: 原子散乱因子データセット (別 family、CC-BY-4.0)。DOI は未発行 (Zenodo は作者判断) —
  #   空の doi や仮の DOI を書かない (CFF 1.2.0 では doi は任意)。発行後にここへ追記する。
  - type: data
    title: >-
      Atomic X-ray and first-Born electron scattering factors f_x(s), f_e(s) for
      86 neutral atoms (Z = 1-86), computed with Temari
    authors:
      - family-names: Seto
        given-names: Yusuke
    version: "1.0.0"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/seto77/Temari/releases/tag/dataset-factors-v1.0.0"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: >-
      dataset-factors v1.0.0, released separately from this software and from the
      F(s, E0) dataset, under CC-BY-4.0. No DOI has been assigned yet; cite this
      versioned GitHub release and identify the archive by its published SHA-256
      when exact byte-level reproducibility matters. The archive is
      self-contained (schema, manifest, golden vectors and an executable
      reference loader).
  # ⚠ 260811Cl 訂正: 題名・巻号・DOI がまとめて誤っていた。
  #   正しくは ADNDT **95**(6), 871-909 (2009), doi 10.1016/j.adt.2009.08.001 (出版社の書誌で照合)。
  #   旧記載の doi 10.1016/j.adt.2010.06.001 は**バリウム同位体の発見**という無関係な論文を指す。
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Cross sections for ionization of K, L and M shells of atoms by impact of
      electrons and positrons with energies up to 1 GeV: Analytical formulas
    authors:
      - family-names: Bote
        given-names: David
      - family-names: Salvat
        given-names: Francesc
      - family-names: Jablonski
        given-names: Aleksander
      - family-names: Powell
        given-names: Cedric J.
    journal: "Atomic Data and Nuclear Data Tables"
    volume: 95
    start: 871
    end: 909
    year: 2009
    doi: "10.1016/j.adt.2009.08.001"
    notes: >-
      Source of the bundled absolute ionization cross-section parameterization
      (src/bote_salvat.json). See also the Erratum, At. Data Nucl. Data Tables
      97, 186 (2011).
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Calculations of inner-shell ionization by electron impact with the
      distorted-wave and plane-wave Born approximations
    authors:
      - family-names: Bote
        given-names: David
      - family-names: Salvat
        given-names: Francesc
    journal: "Physical Review A"
    volume: 77
    start: 042701
    year: 2008
    doi: "10.1103/PhysRevA.77.042701"
    notes: >-
      The relativistic distorted-wave calculations that the bundled
      parameterization was fitted to.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Relativistic EELS scattering cross-sections for microanalysis based on
      Dirac solutions
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhang
        given-names: Zezhong
      - family-names: Lobato
        given-names: Ivan
      - family-names: Brown
        given-names: Hamish
      - family-names: Lamoen
        given-names: Dirk
      - family-names: Jannis
        given-names: Daen
      - family-names: Verbeeck
        given-names: Johan
      - family-names: Van Aert
        given-names: Sandra
      - family-names: Nellist
        given-names: Peter D.
    year: 2024
    doi: "10.48550/arXiv.2405.10151"
    notes: >-
      No code, parameters or tabulated values from this work are bundled here.
      It is cited because (a) the relativistic-electrodynamics interaction
      kernel, the small-component radial matrix element and the kappa-resolved
      angular factor are implemented from the equations as presented in this
      paper (equations 38-41; the underlying physics is standard relativistic
      scattering theory, and equation 38 as printed is missing a q^2 in the
      transverse denominator, corrected here and cross-checked against the
      paper's own equation 42), and (b) the authors' open Dirac GOS database
      (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.7729585, CC-BY) is used as an external comparison
      target during verification. The database itself is not redistributed.
